@startuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false

actor "RooCode Agent" as Agent
actor "User" as User
participant "System (Project & Cosmic Ray)" as System

title Sequence Diagram: Run Basic Mutation Test

autonumber

Agent -> System: Navigate to submodule (repos/<project_name>)
Agent -> System: // Precondition: Cosmic Ray installed (ref. UC 01.1)
Agent -> System: Run project test suite (e.g., pytest)
System --> Agent: Test results (Pass/Fail)

break Tests Fail
    System --> Agent: Report Failure
    Agent --> User: Notify: Mutation testing stopped due to failing tests
end

note over Agent, System: Process continues only if tests PASS

Agent -> User: Request configuration preferences (Distributor: Local/HTTP, Method: Interactive/Manual)
User -> Agent: Select Distributor (Local/HTTP) and Method (Interactive/Manual)

alt Local Distributor (UC 01.2.1) selected
    alt Interactive Configuration selected
        Agent -> System: Execute 'cosmic-ray new-config cosmic-ray.toml'
        activate System
        note right of User: User interacts directly with the terminal wizard
        System -> User: Prompt for module path, timeout, test command...
        User -> System: Type configuration values
        System --> Agent: Process finishes (cosmic-ray.toml created)
        deactivate System
    else Manual Configuration selected
        Agent -> System: Create cosmic-ray.toml (write file directly)
    end
    Agent -> System: Finalize local configuration
else HTTP Distributor (UC 01.2.2) selected
    alt Interactive Configuration selected
        Agent -> System: Execute 'cosmic-ray new-config cosmic-ray.toml'
        activate System
        note right of User: User interacts directly with the terminal wizard
        System -> User: Prompt for module path, timeout, test command...
        User -> System: Type configuration values
        System --> Agent: Process finishes (cosmic-ray.toml created)
        deactivate System
    else Manual Configuration selected
        Agent -> System: Create cosmic-ray.toml (write file directly)
    end
    Agent -> System: Update cosmic-ray.toml with HTTP worker URLs
    User -> System: Start HTTP worker processes (external action in new terminal)
    System --> System: HTTP workers running
end

Agent -> System: git add .
Agent -> System: git commit -m "build: Add Cosmic Ray configuration"
Agent -> System: cosmic-ray init --force cosmic-ray.toml session.sqlite
Agent -> System: cosmic-ray exec cosmic-ray.toml session.sqlite
activate System
System --> Agent: Mutation test execution results
deactivate System

Agent -> System: cr-report session.sqlite
System --> Agent: Mutation test report
Agent -> User: Present mutation test results
Agent -> System: Deactivate virtual environment
Agent -> System: cd ../.. (Return to workspace root)

@enduml
